In article <1991Apr19.145228.15942@digibd.com> merlyn@digibd.com (Merlyn LeRoy) writes:
>The problem is this; you zap an unknown wand, once.  It is fire.
>Now, is it REALLY fire, or a wand of wonder/everything?
>You can't be sure until you've definitely identified which wand
>is the wand of wonder/everything.  This is for EVERY wand you
>identify by one zap...

Yes, but with there being only 1 wand to worry about, I will assume my first
zap/whatever is correct.  I will eventually figure out which one is the WoE,
but I will not use extra charges because of the WoE's existence.  It may be
an inconveniance once, but only hasty people will suffer using this method.

Also, I am only concerned with certain wands (WoE would not be among them),
and if the WoE mimicked something I could care less about, it would cease to
be a problem.  This means that there is a good chance that I will disregard
the WoE after one use.

>It also has a couple of other bizarre attributes that I
>won't reveal here...

I read somewhere in this newsgroup that the WoE was going to be in the next
release.  I had also thought it was meant to replace a WoP.  I would like to
know if the above are correct.  If so, I want to know what its other bizarre
attributes will be.

My view is if you want a WoE, fine.  It is not, however, a solution to the
polypile problem and should not replace a WoP.


About polypiling
----------------
Still, I think it is unnecessary to change the wand of polymorph.  If it must
be changed, making it like a wand of wishing is all that needs to be done.

1) you can not create a wand of polymorph by polymorphing a wand
2) you can only recharge it once

The probability of finding a WoP should remain the same as it is now.
